BT /FB 21 Tf 0.0 g 56.0 773.89 Td (2. Three ways to host it) Tj ET
0.8 G 0.6 w 56.0 765.89 m 539.28 765.89 l S
BT /FB 14 Tf 0.0 g 56.0 731.89 Td (A. Single host, everything in Docker  \(recommended\)) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 715.89 Td (One VPS running docker-compose.prod.yml. Caddy terminates TLS on 443; every other service binds to localhost) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 702.89 Td (or stays on the compose network. This is what the repository is already built for.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 686.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 686.89 Td (Cost: roughly $20-40/month for 4-8 GB RAM \(Hetzner, DigitalOcean, Linode\).) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 671.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 671.89 Td (Web and workers share a private network - no public hop, no egress cost.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 656.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 656.89 Td (One deploy target, one secret store, one place to read logs.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 641.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 641.89 Td (Against it: you own the machine. Backups, patching, and a reboot are yours.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 626.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 626.89 Td (Scaling is vertical until it isn't - a bigger box, not more boxes.) Tj ET
BT /FB 14 Tf 0.0 g 56.0 595.89 Td (B. Managed everything, split tiers) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 579.89 Td (Vercel for the web tier, a PaaS for the Python tier, and managed data services. No servers to patch, at the cost of) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 566.89 Td (six vendors and public hops between tiers that used to be private calls.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 550.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 550.89 Td (Cost: realistically $60-120/month once past free tiers.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 535.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 535.89 Td (Vercel Hobby cannot run this: crons are once-daily and functions cap at 60s.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 520.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 520.89 Td (Every tier boundary becomes an authenticated internet call.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 505.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 505.89 Td (For it: genuinely no ops, and the web tier autoscales.) Tj ET
BT /FB 14 Tf 0.0 g 56.0 474.89 Td (C. One PaaS for everything) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 458.89 Td (Railway or Render running the web tier, the Python services, and managed Postgres and Redis in one project, on) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 445.89 Td (one private network.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 429.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 429.89 Td (Cost: roughly $40-80/month.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 414.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 414.89 Td (Keeps private networking and a single vendor; skips server maintenance.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.45 g 56.0 399.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 70.0 399.89 Td (The reasonable middle if you do not want to own a VPS.) Tj ET
BT /FB 11 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 368.89 Td (Recommendation) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 354.89 Td (Start with A. The compose file, the TLS proxy, the health gate and the rollback path already exist and are tested.) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 341.89 Td (Move to C if machine maintenance becomes the thing you dislike most. Choose B only if something outside) Tj ET
BT /FR 9.5 Tf 0.15 g 56.0 328.89 Td (engineering requires Vercel.) Tj ET
BT /FR 8 Tf 0.55 g 479.28 42.0 Td (3 / 7) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
